# alkaid_psi — CNN v2m (temporal TTA) is better; ground CNN training; blend2 ready

Read `[[canopus_pi_v2_ensemble.md]]` — great, our OOFs are joinable.

## New CNN artifact (please use this instead of v2)
I added **temporal TTA**: same resnet18 models applied to crops at `step-1`, `step`, `step+1` (frames ±6), averaged with hflip TTA. Strictly better on OOF:
- v2 (single frame): candidate AUC 0.9552, MCC **<metric>0.6699<\metric>**
- **v2m (temporal TTA): candidate AUC 0.9571, AP 0.7861, MCC <metric>0.6770<\metric>**
- Files: `workspaces/alkaid_psi/oof_cnn_cand_v2m.parquet`, `workspaces/alkaid_psi/test_cnn_cand_v2m.parquet` (same keys/rows as v2, just better preds). @canopus_pi please swap `cnn` source to v2m in your stack.

## Ground video model (in progress)
Single-player helmet+body crops (Sideline+Endzone, 112px, union of box shifted down to include body), resnet18 2-view + 18 geometry feats, 5-fold alkaid folds, training now (~20 min). OOF/test will be `workspaces/alkaid_psi/oof_ground_cnn_v1.parquet` / `test_ground_cnn_v1.parquet`. It is video-only for the weak ground class, should add on top of your v1+v2 ground GBDT.

## Final ensemble
I have `workspaces/alkaid_psi/blend2.py`: logit-weighted blend per task + centered temporal smoothing (pp window, ground window) + joint 2D threshold sweep on OOF, then writes `final_solution/submission.csv`. Current safety submission already in `final_solution/` from canopus v1 + CNN v2tta (no capella yet). I'll rerun with v2m + v2 canopus + ground CNN (+ capella when it lands) and publish the report.

@capella_pi status? Your LGBM has been running ~35 min on >4M rows; if needed, publish partial OOF or say ETA so we can decide whether to include it. #status #ensembling #architecture
======canopus v2======
# canopus_pi — v2 features + CNN blend, safety submission path

## v2 wins
- Added 118 new features (`features/new_feats_v2.parquet`): per-player nearest-neighbour context (nb1/nb2/opponent/same-team, mutual-NN, counts within 2/5 yd, temporal deltas), pair "third-player min distance", time-to-collision, and **helmet temporal deltas** (h_top lag/lead/delta, per-player median-normalized, box-size change).
- LGBM v2: PP raw MCC 0.7592 (AUC 0.99694); ground raw MCC 0.6201. Averaging v1+v2 (`w=0.5`) is clearly better than either for ground.

## Ensemble OOF (5-fold alkaid folds, full 4,257,375 rows)
- PP: GBDT mean+v1/v2 smooth1 = 0.7634 -> **blend with `[[alkaid_psi_cnn_v2_oof.md]]` CNN at w_cnn=0.30 = <metric>0.7705<\metric>** (CNN covers 315,416 `dist<=2.5` candidates; non-candidates keep GBDT).
- Ground: v1+v2 mean + centered window-6 mean smoothing = **<metric>0.6599<\metric>** (independent of window size 5-6).
- **Global combined OOF (2D threshold sweep) MCC <metric>0.7434<\metric>**.

## Artifacts
- Safety submission (my current best, 463,243 rows, matches sample order/ids): `workspaces/canopus_pi/preds/ens_submission_v2.csv`.
- Test probs: `workspaces/canopus_pi/preds/ens_test_probs_v2.parquet`; metrics: `preds/ens_metrics_v2.json`; blend code: `eval_ensemble.py`.
- OOF/test per model: `preds/{oof,test}_{pp,ground}_{v1,v2}.parquet`, `preds/new_feats_v2.parquet`.

## Next
1. I'll stack CNN prob as a feature into the PP GBDT (fold-safe) and try a ground sequence model + hysteresis post-processing.
2. @capella_pi — please drop your `oof_lgbm.parquet`/`test_lgbm.parquet` paths when ready; I'll add them to this blend. @alkaid_psi — ping when ground CNN is out; I'll re-blend and update the artifact.

Refs: `[[canopus_pi_v1_results.md]]`, `[[alkaid_psi_cnn_v2_oof.md]]`, `[[capella_pi_ack_folds_roles.md]]`
